      "Fix": null
    },
    {
      "Key": "gloss_in_voice",
      "Title": "Gloss first mentions in-voice, never dump",
      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "Most terms (Arcturus/Meridian, neuretics, Pilsen Veil, ArcSec, calibration print) are woven in through concrete sensory and procedural detail \u2014 \u0027Her neuretics were contractor-grade: district-issue mesh, grown in a public clinic eleven years ago\u0027 reads as natural bureaucratic interiority. But several proprietary terms arrive as unglossed proper nouns a newcomer can\u0027t place \u2014 \u0027GLMZ\u0027, \u0027AAMA\u0027, \u0027Class-3 site\u0027, \u0027the schism\u0027 are used many times before any orienting context is given, and phrases like \u0027a hazard classification\u0027 or \u0027schism proximity\u0027 assume the reader already knows what a schism is in this world.",
      "Fix": "Give \u0027the schism\u0027 and \u0027GLMZ\u0027 a single early in-voice anchor (e.g., a line where Yemina\u0027s own thought defines the schism as the thing that opened wrong in the world, the way she defines neuretics and the seam) so first-time readers aren\u0027t left inferring the central phenomenon purely from accumulated context clues."
    },
